    "summary": "Explosive Dark Star > Bird Song, tight jams and classic rockers",
    "blurb": "The set opens with a soaring Playin' → Dark Star → Bird Song stretch that highlights Jerry’s incendiary leads and Phil’s thunderous bass. Standout moments include the seamless China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider segue, Uncle John's Band and Pigpen’s gritty Big Boss Man. The entire performance runs high‑energy with crisp soundboard capture available.",
    "review": "July 31 1971 at the Yale Bowl captures the Dead in a rare moment of pure inspiration. From the first set the band launches into a Playin' → Dark Star → Bird Song sequence that feels both expansive and tightly focused – Jerry’s guitar blazes, Phil’s bass paints with wild brushstrokes, and Bill drives the groove with massive, out‑of‑control fills. After a handful of early‑’70 staples the second set delivers classic chemistry: China Cat Sunflower seamlessly flows into I Know You Rider, Uncle John's Band builds to an exuberant climax, and Pigpen’s raw blues swagger on Big Boss Man and Johnny B. Goode adds gritty fire. The show maintains a soaring momentum throughout, making it one of the most compelling early‑’70 performances, especially with the superbly restored Miller soundboard recording that captures every nuance.",
